# Frontend configuration. Copy to frontend/.env (git-ignored) and edit if needed.
# Nothing here is a secret, and no AWS/Gemini credentials belong in the frontend.

# Where the browser sends /api requests.
#   unset                 -> direct calls to http://localhost:8000 (backend CORS allows "*")
#   (empty value)         -> same-origin "/api" via the Vite dev proxy in vite.config.ts
#   http://host:port      -> point the UI at a backend on a different host/port
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=

# OPTIONAL, display-only override for the dashboard's "reference today" label.
# The backend plans against the REAL current date, so normal users should leave
# this UNSET and rely on the device clock. Only set it for a fixed-date demo.
# VITE_DEMO_TODAY=YYYY-MM-DD

# Dashboard-only mock source (M5). Truthy values (1/true/yes/on) make the
# Today / Upcoming / Conflicts panels read browser-generated fixtures instead
# of the backend, so the UI can be built and tested with no server running.
# While it is on, the page shows a persistent "Demo data" banner and badge, and
# invented fields such as estimated hours are labelled as synthetic.
# The Assistant chat is NOT mocked — it still requires the backend.
# VITE_DEMO_MODE=true

# How long the demo source waits before answering, in milliseconds (default 350).
# Raise it to make the panels' first-paint skeletons observable in a browser —
# a normal round-trip is slower than 350 ms, so the loading state is otherwise
# impossible to catch by hand. Demo-only: the real API path never reads this.
# VITE_DEMO_LATENCY_MS=60000
